    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="0928" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.801/40</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1592. Admiralty announcement canceling notice on navigation North Sea of November
                    30, 1914, cabled by Skinner May 17<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d929-f1"/> states that British and Allied vessels wishing to
                    use northabout route should apply to customs, and neutral vessels must apply for
                    permission, through their foreign representatives, and failing such permission
                    proceed southabout.</p>
                <pb facs="0929" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/>
                <p>Department does not fully understand the intention and effect underlying such
                    regulations, and shall be glad to have an immediate report on the subject from
                    you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d929-f1" n="1" xml:id="d929-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram not printed. It summarizes the notice enclosed in the Consul General’s
                    despatch of May 19.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
